      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 0,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Exercise: homography estimation with RANSAC and local features\n\nTwo photos of the same planar object (here a boxed product seen among clutter vs. a clean frontal shot). The 'Feature Match + RANSAC Homography' subgraph detects ORB features in both images, matches them with a brute-force matcher + Lowe ratio test, and estimates the homography with 'CV Find Homography (RANSAC)' (reprojection threshold 3 px). The estimation is failure-tolerant: with too few matches it outputs found=false and an identity homography instead of stopping the workflow. Image A is then warped onto image B's frame (cv2.warpPerspective, output size taken from image B via 'CV Array Size') and blended 50/50 with cv2.addWeighted - if the homography is right, the two images line up in the overlay.\n\nDebug outputs: the side-by-side inlier match drawing, the 3x3 homography matrix ('Inspect CV Data') and the RANSAC inlier count. Everything between the loaders and the previews stays in raw ndarray form - no tensor round trips."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
